{"id":"9cf4c10a-32a2-42d2-b395-dbc2800ce456","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0b16e9a65c70ecbe","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/shell/git-push.ts","baseline":{"blob":"6aec63c4db2c1a8970b6a4ff48941f7467dcdef0","start":0,"end":73},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","RemoteRequest",",","RemoteResponse","}","from","\"","../shared/git-remote","\""]},"context":{"after":"0f7c1c676a768f5a"}},"payload":{"text":"A push from the workspace's git (workbench/git-engine.ts), through the API's proxy (packages/api/README.md, *The\nproxy*). The workbench's isomorphic-git makes the requests — it has the repository — and the shell sends them, as only\nthe shell holds the sign-in (its DPoP key, session.ts): each comes over the hub as `git.remote`, for a github.com\nrepository, and goes to the proxy, which adds GitHub's token. The bytes cross; no credential does. Signed out, or\nsigned in without GitHub, there's no push, and the answer says so.\n\nAnd who a commit is by (`git.identity`): the signed-in GitHub user, with GitHub's no-reply address — what the\nworkspace's commits are authored as, so a pushed one is theirs.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:47:17.726Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:47:17.726Z"}
